#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:5
#: dbb9024d67c34c1291b0ede277660241
msgid "SWAN-K1 HWing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:7
#: 010ff4cbdc0c4505acfcb2dbbdf60e5c
msgid "This autopilot is a part of a :ref:`ready-to-fly vehicle <common-rtf>` in  the form of a control-surfaceless, quad-copter Tailsitter QuadPlane. It comes with customized PX4 firmware installed and an GCS application that is downloadable for smart phones. This page describes the conversion to ArduPilot firmware and its setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:9
#: 9f59d1604d764eff808d1ed798ffb151
msgid "It was initially offered with a 10 channel RC transmitter using an external smart phone for GCS and video display, and the Pro version comes with a 12 channel system with an integrated screen for the GCS/Video."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:14
#: 46d20088c4ee4d4d8640872d03184b2e
msgid "ArduPilot Firmware Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:16
#: 08774d7edc10442abf3c5525daa5b22b
msgid "You will need to remove the access cover in order to attach a USB cable to the autopilot. Installing a short 90 deg USB pigtail, routed into the battery compartment will allow easy USB connections in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:21
#: 2ec8a2bd1c93482db8727893cc492725
msgid "Connect to Mission Planner or QGC, and upload the Plane firmware for the SWAN-K1 located `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:23
#: e75a71476c8c4a459dfc240e91d893b3
msgid "The firmware has defaults already set for optimum tuning and operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:26
#: 39cbbc797e55459baa72cb0dab5844ad
msgid "Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-Swan-K1.rst:28
#: df39e91b2b3d40b589530c64425aa7c7
msgid "Once the new ArduPilot firmware is loaded, you will only need to :ref:`calibrate the accelerometers <common-accelerometer-calibration>` and :ref:`calibrate the compass<common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>`. The level point for the accelerometer calibration should be normal fixed wing flight attitude."
msgstr ""

